@*
    One order, at "/order/{orderNumber}?token=…".

    THE TIMELINE IS THE POINT. Everything else on this page is a receipt; the rail is the demo.
    An order placed here is advanced from Paid to Packed to Shipped by background workers that
    know nothing about the request that created it, and watching that happen — on a page nobody
    reloaded — is the thing this whole project exists to show.

    THE TOKEN IS WHY THE LINK WORKS ANYWHERE. `token` is a signed capability for this one order,
    so the page opens in a browser with no session, on another device, after cleared cookies. It
    is not tenancy: it names one order and expires. Without it the endpoint falls back to "does
    this order belong to the calling session", which is the ordinary path immediately after a
    checkout in the same tab — so a token-less /order/VELA-XXXXXXX still works for the shopper
    who just placed it, and 404s for everybody else.

    POLLING IS BOUNDED IN THREE DIRECTIONS, because a page left open is a page that keeps a
    serverless database awake and billing:
      * it stops when the order reaches a terminal state, since nothing will change again;
      * it stops when the tab is hidden, and refreshes the moment it comes back;
      * it slows down and then stops on a schedule (OrderProgress.NextPollDelay), leaving a
        Refresh button, because an order still Pending after half an hour is the Abandon
        scenario and no amount of asking will move it.
    And it stops when this component is disposed, which is what the cancellation token is for.
*@
@page "/order/{OrderNumber}"
@using Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection
@using VelaCommerce.Storefront.Cart
@using VelaCommerce.Storefront.Checkout
@implements IAsyncDisposable
@inject HttpClient Http
@inject NavigationManager Nav
@inject IJSRuntime JS
@inject IServiceProvider Services

<PageTitle>@DocumentTitle</PageTitle>

<nav class="vc-crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
    <a class="vc-crumbs__link" href="">Catalog</a>
    <span class="vc-crumbs__sep" aria-hidden="true">/</span>
    <span>Order</span>
</nav>

@if (_order is null && _notFound)
{
    <div class="vc-empty">
        <span class="vc-eyebrow">Not found</span>
        <h1 class="vc-empty__title">This link does not open an order</h1>
        <p class="vc-empty__body">
            The shop answers a wrong order number, an expired link and somebody else's order in
            exactly the same way, on purpose &mdash; so that the difference between two error
            messages cannot be used to find out which order numbers exist. Any of the three could
            be what happened here.
        </p>
        <p class="vc-empty__body">
            A confirmation link stays valid for thirty days. If you placed this order in this
            browser, opening it without the <code class="vc-code">token</code> in the address will
            work too.
        </p>
        <div class="vc-alert__actions">
            <a class="vc-btn vc-btn--primary" href="">Back to the catalog</a>
        </div>
    </div>
}
else if (_order is null && _error is { Length: > 0 } fatal)
{
    <div class="vc-alert vc-alert--error" role="alert">
        <h1 class="vc-alert__title">@fatal</h1>
        <p class="vc-alert__body">
            The order is safe &mdash; this is the shop being unreachable, not the order being gone.
            Nothing about it changes while this page cannot read it.
        </p>
        @if (_errorDetail is { Length: > 0 } fatalDetail)
        {
            <details class="vc-alert__detail">
                <summary>Technical detail</summary>
                @fatalDetail
            </details>
        }
        <div class="vc-alert__actions">
            <button type="button" class="vc-btn vc-btn--primary" disabled="@_loading" @onclick="RefreshAsync">Try again</button>
            <a class="vc-btn" href="">Back to the catalog</a>
        </div>
    </div>
}
else if (_order is null)
{
    <div class="vc-waking" role="status" aria-live="polite">
        <span class="vc-waking__pip" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <div class="vc-waking__body">
            <p class="vc-waking__title">@(_waking ? "Waking the shop up" : "Opening your order")</p>
            <p class="vc-waking__note">
                The API sleeps when nothing is happening, so the first request after a quiet period
                waits for it to start. Your order is unaffected either way.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>
}
else
{
    var order = _order;

    <div class="vc-hero">
        <span class="vc-eyebrow">Order</span>
        <h1 class="vc-section-title vc-tabular">@order.OrderNumber</h1>
        <div class="vc-hero__meta">
            <span class="vc-tag @StatusTag()">@OrderProgress.Label(_stage)</span>
            <span>Placed @LongClock(order.PlacedAt)</span>
            <span>@order.TotalQuantity @(order.TotalQuantity == 1 ? "item" : "items")</span>
        </div>
    </div>

    @* One live region for the whole page, so a screen reader is told the order moved without
       having to go and look for the rail. *@
    <p class="vc-visually-hidden" role="status" aria-live="polite">@_announcement</p>

    @if (_stage == OrderStage.Cancelled)
    {
        @* Deliberately not styled as an error. An order can be cancelled for entirely ordinary
           reasons — a refused card is the commonest — and a page that shouts about it is the
           page being wrong, not the order. *@
        <div class="vc-notice" role="status">
            <h2 class="vc-notice__title">This order was cancelled</h2>
            @* Two cancellations reach this banner and they are not the same fact. A refused card
               never charged anything; a cancellation after payment charged and gave it back. The
               copy used to say "nothing was charged" for both, which was true until refunds made
               the second path reachable and then read as a denial that the money had ever moved. *@
            <p class="vc-notice__body">
                @if (_order?.Refunded is { Amount: > 0 } returned)
                {
                    <text>
                        @Money(returned) went back to the card it came from, and the reserved stock is
                        back on the shelf.
                    </text>
                }
                else
                {
                    <text>Nothing was charged and the reserved stock has gone back on the shelf.</text>
                }
                The order stays readable at this address; it simply will not move any further.
            </p>
        </div>
    }
    else if (_stage == OrderStage.Pending)
    {
        <div class="vc-notice" role="status">
            <h2 class="vc-notice__title">
                @(_payment?.AwaitsSettlement == true ? "Confirming payment" : "Waiting for payment")
            </h2>
            <p class="vc-notice__body">
                @if (_payment?.AwaitsSettlement == true)
                {
                    <text>
                        The gateway accepted the order and will settle it with a signed notification in a
                        moment. Until that lands the money has genuinely not moved, so this page says
                        pending rather than showing you a receipt. It updates itself.
                    </text>
                }
                else
                {
                    <text>
                        The order exists and its stock is reserved, but no payment has settled against it.
                        If the payment was never finished, the reservation lapses on its own and the units
                        go back on the shelf.
                    </text>
                }
            </p>
        </div>
    }

    <section class="vc-order__progress" aria-labelledby="vc-order-progress-title">
        <div class="vc-order__section-head">
            <h2 class="vc-order__section-title" id="vc-order-progress-title">Progress</h2>
            <p class="vc-order__watch" role="status" aria-live="polite">@WatchStatus()</p>
        </div>

        <OrderTimeline Stage="_stage"
                       PlacedAt="order.PlacedAt"
                       PaidAt="order.PaidAt"
                       Observed="_observed" />

        <p class="vc-order__aside">
            Packing and shipping are driven by a background worker on a timer, not by anything this
            page does. Nothing is being simulated in your browser &mdash; close the tab, come back
            tomorrow, and the order will have moved on without you.
        </p>

        @if (_watchStopped || _pollNote is { Length: > 0 })
        {
            <div class="vc-order__watch-actions">
                @if (_pollNote is { Length: > 0 } pollNote)
                {
                    <p class="vc-order__watch-note">@pollNote</p>
                }
                <button type="button" class="vc-btn vc-btn--sm" disabled="@_loading" @onclick="RefreshAsync">
                    Check again
                </button>
            </div>
        }
    </section>

    <div class="vc-order__grid">
        <section class="vc-order__panel" aria-labelledby="vc-order-lines-title">
            <h2 class="vc-order__section-title" id="vc-order-lines-title">What you bought</h2>

            <ul class="vc-summary__lines">
                @foreach (var line in order.Lines ?? [])
                {
                    <li class="vc-summary__line" @key="line.Sku">
                        <div class="vc-summary__line-main">
                            <span class="vc-summary__name">@line.DisplayName</span>
                            <span class="vc-summary__meta">
                                <span class="vc-tabular">@line.Sku</span>
                                <span aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span>
                                <span class="vc-tabular">&times;@line.Quantity</span>
                                <span aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span>
                                <span class="vc-tabular">@Money(line.UnitPrice) each</span>
                            </span>
                        </div>
                        <PriceTag Money="line.LineTotal" />
                    </li>
                }
            </ul>

            <hr class="vc-rule" />

            <dl class="vc-totals">
                <div class="vc-totals__row">
                    <dt>Subtotal</dt>
                    <dd class="vc-tabular">@Money(order.Subtotal)</dd>
                </div>
                <div class="vc-totals__row">
                    <dt>Shipping</dt>
                    <dd class="vc-tabular">@Money(order.Shipping)</dd>
                </div>
                <div class="vc-totals__row">
                    <dt>Tax</dt>
                    <dd class="vc-tabular">@Money(order.Tax)</dd>
                </div>
                <div class="vc-totals__row vc-totals__row--total">
                    <dt>Total</dt>
                    <dd class="vc-tabular">@Money(order.Total)</dd>
                </div>
                <div class="vc-totals__row">
                    <dt>Captured</dt>
                    <dd class="vc-tabular">@Money(order.Captured)</dd>
                </div>
                @if (order.Refunded is { Amount: > 0 })
                {
                    <div class="vc-totals__row">
                        <dt>Refunded</dt>
                        <dd class="vc-tabular">@Money(order.Refunded)</dd>
                    </div>
                }
            </dl>

            <p class="vc-order__aside">
                @if (order.Captured is { Amount: 0 } && _stage is not OrderStage.Cancelled)
                {
                    <text>
                        Captured is what the gateway has actually taken, and it is zero until settlement
                        completes. It is shown beside the total rather than instead of it, because
                        "owed" and "paid" are two different facts and a receipt that conflates them is a
                        receipt for money that may not exist.
                    </text>
                }
                else
                {
                    <text>
                        Every price here was captured at checkout, after the shop revalidated it against
                        the live catalog. This order reads the same a year from now whatever happens to
                        those products.
                    </text>
                }
            </p>
        </section>

        @if (ShowMoneyBack)
        {
            <section class="vc-order__panel" aria-labelledby="vc-order-refunds-title">
                <h2 class="vc-order__section-title" id="vc-order-refunds-title">Money back</h2>

                @if (order.Refunds is { Count: > 0 } ledger)
                {
                    <dl class="vc-totals">
                        @foreach (var entry in ledger)
                        {
                            <div class="vc-totals__row">
                                <dt>
                                    @(entry.Reason == "Cancellation" ? "Cancelled" : "Refunded")
                                    <span class="vc-order__aside">
                                        @entry.RefundedAt.ToLocalTime().ToString("d MMM, HH:mm")
                                        @if (entry.Restocked)
                                        {
                                            <text> &middot; @entry.RestockedUnits back on the shelf</text>
                                        }
                                    </span>
                                </dt>
                                <dd class="vc-tabular">@Money(entry.Amount)</dd>
                            </div>
                        }
                        <div class="vc-totals__row vc-totals__row--total">
                            <dt>Still owed</dt>
                            <dd class="vc-tabular"><PriceTag Money="order.RefundableRemaining" /></dd>
                        </div>
                    </dl>
                }

                @if (_moneyError is { Length: > 0 } moneyError)
                {
                    <div class="vc-alert vc-alert--error" role="alert">
                        <p class="vc-alert__title">@moneyError</p>
                        @if (_moneyErrorDetail is { Length: > 0 } moneyDetail)
                        {
                            <details class="vc-alert__detail">
                                <summary>Technical detail</summary>
                                @moneyDetail
                            </details>
                        }
                    </div>
                }
                else if (_moneyNote is { Length: > 0 } moneyNote)
                {
                    <p class="vc-order__aside" role="status">@moneyNote</p>
                }

                @if (CanRefund || CanCancel)
                {
                    <div class="vc-alert__actions">
                        @if (CanRefund)
                        {
                            <button type="button"
                                    class="vc-btn vc-btn--primary"
                                    disabled="@_moneyBusy"
                                    @onclick="RefundOrderAsync">
                                Refund @Money(order.Captured is null ? null : new MoneyDocument
                                {
                                    Amount = order.RefundableRemaining?.AmountMinorUnits ?? 0,
                                    Currency = order.Currency,
                                })
                            </button>
                        }
                        @if (CanCancel)
                        {
                            <button type="button"
                                    class="vc-btn"
                                    disabled="@_moneyBusy"
                                    @onclick="CancelOrderAsync">
                                Cancel order
                            </button>
                        }
                    </div>
                }

                <p class="vc-order__aside">
                    @if (CanCancel && order.RefundableRemaining is { AmountMinorUnits: > 0 })
                    {
                        <text>
                            Cancelling returns the money and puts the units back on the shelf as one
                            act, because an order cannot be left terminated while it still owes:
                            a cancelled order refuses refunds, so the money would be unreachable.
                        </text>
                    }
                    else if (_stage is OrderStage.Shipped)
                    {
                        <text>
                            The parcel has gone, so this order can be refunded but not cancelled.
                            It keeps saying Shipped afterwards &mdash; the goods really are in the
                            world, and a status that hid that would be lying about where they are.
                        </text>
                    }
                    else if (order.IsFullyRefunded)
                    {
                        <text>
                            Every cent is back. The shop asked the gateway first and wrote the line
                            above only once it confirmed, so a row here always means money that
                            actually moved.
                            @if (CanCancel)
                            {
                                <text>
                                    Cancelling now owes nothing and only releases the stock &mdash;
                                    which is why it is allowed at all: the rule is that an order may
                                    not be cancelled while it still holds money, not that a paid
                                    order may never be cancelled.
                                </text>
                            }
                        </text>
                    }
                    else
                    {
                        <text>
                            Refunds are issued against the payment rather than the order, and the
                            same request sent twice returns the money once &mdash; the key that
                            makes that true is generated here, not by you.
                        </text>
                    }
                </p>
            </section>
        }

        <section class="vc-order__panel" aria-labelledby="vc-order-address-title">
            <h2 class="vc-order__section-title" id="vc-order-address-title">Shipping to</h2>

            @if (order.ShippingAddress is { } address)
            {
                <address class="vc-address">
                    <span class="vc-address__line vc-address__line--name">@address.Recipient</span>
                    <span class="vc-address__line">@address.Line1</span>
                    @if (address.Line2 is { Length: > 0 } line2)
                    {
                        <span class="vc-address__line">@line2</span>
                    }
                    <span class="vc-address__line">
                        @address.City@(address.Region is { Length: > 0 } region ? $", {region}" : "")
                    </span>
                    <span class="vc-address__line vc-tabular">@address.PostalCode @address.CountryCode</span>
                </address>
            }

            @if (_payment is { } payment)
            {
                <hr class="vc-rule" />
                <h3 class="vc-order__subtitle">What the gateway said</h3>
                <dl class="vc-gateway">
                    <div class="vc-gateway__row">
                        <dt class="vc-gateway__key">Outcome</dt>
                        <dd class="vc-gateway__value">
                            @payment.Outcome@(payment.DeclineReason is { Length: > 0 } reason ? $" — {reason}" : "")
                        </dd>
                    </div>
                    <div class="vc-gateway__row">
                        <dt class="vc-gateway__key">Reference</dt>
                        <dd class="vc-gateway__value vc-tabular">@payment.GatewayReference</dd>
                    </div>
                </dl>
                <p class="vc-order__aside">
                    Reported once, on the response to the checkout that asked for it, and stored nowhere
                    &mdash; so it is on this page only because you have just placed the order. Reloading
                    will not bring it back; the durable facts are the status, the captured amount and the
                    paid-at time above.
                </p>
            }

            <hr class="vc-rule" />

            <h3 class="vc-order__subtitle">Keep this link</h3>
            <p class="vc-order__aside">
                It carries a signed token for this one order, so it opens on any device, in any browser,
                with no account and no cookie &mdash; for thirty days. Which also means anyone you send
                it to can read the order, so treat it like a receipt you would not leave on a train.
            </p>
            <input class="vc-input vc-order__link"
                   type="text"
                   readonly
                   aria-label="Link to this order"
                   value="@BookmarkUrl()"
                   @onfocus="SelectAllAsync"
                   @ref="_linkField" />
        </section>
    </div>
}

@code {
    /// <summary>
    /// How long the first read is given. The same generous allowance the checkout submit gets and
    /// for the same reason: this may be the request that pays for the API to start.
    /// </summary>
    private static readonly TimeSpan FirstLoadDeadline = TimeSpan.FromSeconds(30);

    /// <summary>
    /// How long a poll is given. Much shorter, because there is already an order on screen: a poll
    /// that is taking longer than the interval between polls has nothing useful left to say, and
    /// letting them stack up would turn one slow API into a queue of them.
    /// </summary>
    private static readonly TimeSpan PollDeadline = TimeSpan.FromSeconds(10);

    /// <summary>How long the first read may run before the page admits the shop is asleep.</summary>
    private static readonly TimeSpan WakeNotice = TimeSpan.FromSeconds(2);

    private readonly Dictionary<OrderStage, DateTimeOffset> _observed = [];

    private CheckoutApiClient _api = default!;
    private CheckoutState _checkout = default!;

    private IJSObjectReference? _visibilityModule;
    private DotNetObjectReference<Order>? _self;
    private int? _visibilityHandle;

    private CancellationTokenSource? _polling;
    private DateTimeOffset _watchingSince;

    private OrderDocument? _order;
    private OrderPaymentDocument? _payment;
    private OrderStage _stage = OrderStage.Unknown;
    private ElementReference _linkField;

    private string? _bookmarkToken;
    private string? _announcement;
    private string? _error;
    private string? _errorDetail;
    private string? _pollNote;
    private string? _loadedFor;

    private string? _moneyError;
    private string? _moneyErrorDetail;
    private string? _moneyNote;

    /// <summary>
    /// The key for the refund attempt in flight, kept across a retry and cleared once the money has
    /// moved. That lifetime is the whole point: a shopper pressing Refund again after a timeout is
    /// repeating one intention, and a fresh key would turn it into a second refund. A press after a
    /// success is a new intention and gets a new key.
    /// </summary>
    private string? _moneyKey;

    private bool _notFound;
    private bool _loading;
    private bool _moneyBusy;
    private bool _waking;
    private bool _watchStopped;
    private bool _visible = true;
    private bool _startRequested;

    /// <summary>The order number from the route.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string OrderNumber { get; set; } = "";

    /// <summary>
    /// The signed retrieval token from the query string. Optional: without it the shop falls back to
    /// session ownership, which is what makes a bare <c>/order/VELA-XXXXXXX</c> work for the shopper
    /// who just placed it and 404 for everyone else.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter, SupplyParameterFromQuery(Name = "token")]
    public string? Token { get; set; }

    private string DocumentTitle =>
        _order is null
            ? "Order · Vela Commerce"
            : $"{_order.OrderNumber} · {OrderProgress.Label(_stage)} · Vela Commerce";

    protected override void OnInitialized()
    {
        _api = new CheckoutApiClient(Http);

        // Resolved rather than injected, so a missing AddStorefrontCheckout() registration costs the
        // handoff from the checkout page — the gateway's answer, which exists on no other response —
        // and not the order page itself.
        _checkout = Services.GetService<CheckoutState>() ?? new CheckoutState();
    }

    protected override void OnParametersSet()
    {
        if (string.Equals(_loadedFor, OrderNumber, StringComparison.Ordinal))
        {
            return;
        }

        _loadedFor = OrderNumber;

        StopPolling();
        _observed.Clear();
        _order = null;
        _payment = null;
        _stage = OrderStage.Unknown;
        _bookmarkToken = Token;
        _announcement = null;
        _error = null;
        _errorDetail = null;
        _pollNote = null;
        _notFound = false;
        _watchStopped = false;
        _moneyError = null;
        _moneyErrorDetail = null;
        _moneyNote = null;
        _moneyKey = null;
        _moneyBusy = false;
        _watchingSince = DateTimeOffset.Now;

        // The checkout page hands the freshly placed order over rather than making this page ask for
        // it again — and the gateway's answer comes with it, which no later read can supply. It is
        // taken once: a snapshot re-shown on a second visit could contradict the order it describes.
        if (_checkout.TakeReceipt(OrderNumber) is { } receipt)
        {
            Apply(receipt, watched: false);
            _payment = receipt.Payment;
            _bookmarkToken ??= receipt.RetrievalToken;
        }

        _startRequested = true;
    }

    protected override async Task OnAfterRenderAsync(bool firstRender)
    {
        if (!_startRequested)
        {
            return;
        }

        _startRequested = false;

        // AFTER the first render. The shell — crumbs, heading, waking notice — is on screen before
        // anything is asked of an API that may be starting from cold.
        await SetUpVisibilityAsync();

        if (_order is null)
        {
            await LoadAsync(initial: true);
        }

        StartPolling();
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Imports the visibility module and subscribes to it.
    /// <para>
    /// Wrapped, and deliberately non-fatal. A failed import leaves <c>_visible</c> true, which means
    /// the page polls in a hidden tab exactly as it would have without this file at all. That is a
    /// worse page, not a broken one, and it is not worth an error screen.
    /// </para>
    /// </summary>
    private async Task SetUpVisibilityAsync()
    {
        if (_visibilityModule is not null)
        {
            return;
        }

        try
        {
            _visibilityModule = await JS.InvokeAsync<IJSObjectReference>("import", "./js/order-page.js");
            _self = DotNetObjectReference.Create(this);

            // Asked as well as subscribed: a tab opened in the background is already hidden and no
            // visibilitychange event will ever fire to say so.
            _visible = await _visibilityModule.InvokeAsync<bool>("isVisible");
            _visibilityHandle = await _visibilityModule.InvokeAsync<int>("watch", _self);
        }
        catch (Exception)
        {
            _visibilityModule = null;
        }
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Called from JavaScript when the tab is hidden or shown.
    /// <para>
    /// Hidden stops the polling outright rather than slowing it: a background tab has no reader, and
    /// every request it makes wakes a database that bills by the compute-hour. Shown refreshes
    /// immediately, so coming back to the tab shows where the order actually is rather than where it
    /// was when you left.
    /// </para>
    /// </summary>
    [JSInvokable]
    public async Task OnVisibilityChanged(bool visible)
    {
        await InvokeAsync(async () =>
        {
            _visible = visible;

            if (!visible)
            {
                StopPolling();
                StateHasChanged();
                return;
            }

            StateHasChanged();

            if (_order is not null && !OrderProgress.IsTerminal(_stage) && !_watchStopped)
            {
                await LoadAsync(initial: false);
            }

            StartPolling();
        });
    }

    /// <summary>What the shopper asked for: one read now, and the watch window restarted around it.</summary>
    private async Task RefreshAsync()
    {
        _watchStopped = false;
        _watchingSince = DateTimeOffset.Now;

        await LoadAsync(initial: _order is null);

        StartPolling();
    }

    private async Task LoadAsync(bool initial)
    {
        if (_loading)
        {
            return;
        }

        _loading = true;
        StateHasChanged();

        try
        {
            using var deadline = new CancellationTokenSource(initial ? FirstLoadDeadline : PollDeadline);
            var work = _api.GetOrderAsync(OrderNumber, _bookmarkToken ?? Token, deadline.Token);

            if (initial && await Task.WhenAny(work, Task.Delay(WakeNotice)) != work)
            {
                _waking = true;
                StateHasChanged();
            }

            Apply(await work, watched: !initial);

            _error = null;
            _errorDetail = null;
            _notFound = false;
            _pollNote = null;
        }
        catch (OrderApiException exception)
        {
            Fail(exception.Message, exception.Detail, exception.NotFound);
        }
        catch (Exception exception)
        {
            // A poll is a fire-and-forget task. An exception escaping it would be unobserved, and
            // the page would simply stop updating with nothing on screen to say why.
            Fail("Something went wrong while reading this order.", $"{exception.GetType().Name}: {exception.Message}", notFound: false);
        }
        finally
        {
            _loading = false;
            _waking = false;
            StateHasChanged();
        }
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Records a failure without throwing away a good order.
    /// <para>
    /// A failed poll over an order that is already on screen becomes a quiet line beside a Check
    /// again button. Blanking a correct receipt because one request out of twenty timed out would be
    /// the page doing more damage than the failure did.
    /// </para>
    /// </summary>
    private void Fail(string message, string? detail, bool notFound)
    {
        if (_order is not null)
        {
            _pollNote = notFound
                ? "This link has stopped opening the order — the token may have expired."
                : message;

            // A 404 will stay a 404, so there is nothing left to poll for. The order already on
            // screen stays on screen and the Check again button stays available, because the
            // shopper may be about to paste a fresher link.
            if (notFound)
            {
                _watchStopped = true;
                StopPolling();
            }

            return;
        }

        _error = message;
        _errorDetail = detail;
        _notFound = notFound;
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Takes a fresh order document and works out what changed.
    /// </summary>
    /// <param name="order">What the server just said.</param>
    /// <param name="watched">
    /// True when this page was watching when the change arrived, which is the only thing that makes
    /// a Packed or Shipped timestamp honest — the API records no column for either, so the moment
    /// this page saw it is all there is, and it is labelled "seen" rather than presented as the
    /// shop's own record.
    /// </param>
    /// <summary>
    /// Whether the panel has anything to say: money that could come back, money that already has,
    /// or an order that can still be called off.
    /// </summary>
    private bool ShowMoneyBack =>
        _order is { } order
        && (CanRefund || CanCancel || order.Refunds is { Count: > 0 } || order.Captured is { Amount: > 0 });

    /// <summary>
    /// Mirrors the server's rule rather than guessing at it: Paid, Packed and Shipped can be
    /// refunded, and only while something is left. A button the server would refuse is worse than no
    /// button, because the shopper reads the refusal as the shop being broken.
    /// </summary>
    private bool CanRefund =>
        _order is { } order
        && order.RefundableRemaining is { AmountMinorUnits: > 0 }
        && order.Status is "Paid" or "Packed" or "Shipped";

    /// <summary>
    /// The two states with a legal edge to Cancelled. Packed and Shipped are absent because the
    /// parcel has moved, and cancelling would claim the goods are still here.
    /// </summary>
    private bool CanCancel => _order?.Status is "Pending" or "Paid";

    private Task RefundOrderAsync() =>
        MoveMoneyAsync(
            (api, order, key, token) => api.RefundAsync(order, key, token),
            success: result => result.Replayed
                ? "That refund had already gone through. Nothing was refunded twice."
                : $"Refunded {Money(result.Refunded)}. The gateway confirmed before this was written down.");

    private Task CancelOrderAsync() =>
        MoveMoneyAsync(
            (api, order, key, token) => api.CancelOrderAsync(order, key, token),
            success: result => result.RestockedUnits > 0
                ? $"Cancelled. {result.RestockedUnits} unit(s) went back on the shelf"
                  + (result.Refunded is { Amount: > 0 } money ? $" and {Money(money)} went back to you." : ".")
                : "Cancelled.");

    /// <summary>
    /// The shared half of both buttons: one attempt, the key held across a retry, and the canonical
    /// order re-read afterwards.
    /// <para>
    /// The local update happens before the re-read on purpose. The server's answer is already the
    /// truth about the money, so showing it immediately is honest; the re-read then reconciles the
    /// rest of the page — the timeline, mainly — and a re-read that fails leaves the correct figures
    /// on screen rather than blanking them.
    /// </para>
    /// </summary>
    private async Task MoveMoneyAsync(
        Func<CheckoutApiClient, string, string, CancellationToken, Task<RefundResultDocument>> action,
        Func<RefundResultDocument, string> success)
    {
        if (_moneyBusy || _order is not { } order)
        {
            return;
        }

        _moneyBusy = true;
        _moneyError = null;
        _moneyErrorDetail = null;
        _moneyNote = null;
        StateHasChanged();

        try
        {
            _moneyKey ??= $"vela-{Guid.NewGuid():N}";

            using var deadline = new CancellationTokenSource(FirstLoadDeadline);
            var result = await action(_api, order.OrderNumber, _moneyKey, deadline.Token);

            // Spent. A later press is a new intention and must not reuse it.
            _moneyKey = null;
            _moneyNote = success(result);

            _order = order with
            {
                Status = result.Status,
                Refunded = result.Refunded,
                Refunds = result.Refunds,
            };

            _stage = OrderProgress.Parse(result.Status);
        }
        catch (OrderApiException exception)
        {
            _moneyError = exception.Message;
            _moneyErrorDetail = exception.Detail;

            // Kept only when trying again could still work. A 409 is the world disagreeing and will
            // disagree identically next time, so holding its key would be holding a key for an
            // attempt nobody is going to repeat.
            if (!exception.Retryable)
            {
                _moneyKey = null;
            }
        }
        catch (Exception exception)
        {
            _moneyError = "Something went wrong while moving the money.";
            _moneyErrorDetail = $"{exception.GetType().Name}: {exception.Message}";
        }
        finally
        {
            _moneyBusy = false;
            StateHasChanged();
        }

        // Reconciles the timeline and picks up anything the workers did meanwhile. Deliberately
        // outside the try: a failed re-read must not overwrite the money message above.
        await LoadAsync(initial: false);
    }

    private void Apply(OrderDocument order, bool watched)
    {
        var stage = OrderProgress.Parse(order.Status);

        if (_order is not null && stage != _stage)
        {
            if (watched && stage is OrderStage.Packed or OrderStage.Shipped)
            {
                _observed[stage] = DateTimeOffset.Now;
            }

            _announcement = $"Order {order.OrderNumber} is now {OrderProgress.Label(stage)}.";
        }

        _order = order;
        _stage = stage;

        // Every response mints a new token — Data Protection ciphertext is randomised, and a stable
        // token would be a stable secret — so the first one seen is pinned. Otherwise the bookmark
        // link in the field below would change under the shopper's cursor every three seconds.
        _bookmarkToken ??= order.RetrievalToken;
    }

    private void StartPolling()
    {
        if (_polling is not null
            || _order is null
            || !_visible
            || _watchStopped
            || OrderProgress.IsTerminal(_stage))
        {
            return;
        }

        var source = new CancellationTokenSource();
        _polling = source;

        _ = PollAsync(source.Token);
    }

    private void StopPolling()
    {
        var source = _polling;
        _polling = null;

        source?.Cancel();
        source?.Dispose();
    }

    private async Task PollAsync(CancellationToken cancellationToken)
    {
        while (!cancellationToken.IsCancellationRequested)
        {
            var delay = OrderProgress.NextPollDelay(_stage, DateTimeOffset.Now - _watchingSince);

            if (delay is null)
            {
                _watchStopped = true;
                StopPolling();
                StateHasChanged();

                return;
            }

            try
            {
                await Task.Delay(delay.Value, cancellationToken);
            }
            catch (OperationCanceledException)
            {
                // The tab was hidden, the component was disposed, or the shopper pressed Check
                // again. All three are ordinary and none of them is an error.
                return;
            }

            if (cancellationToken.IsCancellationRequested)
            {
                return;
            }

            await LoadAsync(initial: false);

            if (OrderProgress.IsTerminal(_stage))
            {
                StopPolling();
                StateHasChanged();

                return;
            }
        }
    }

    private string WatchStatus()
    {
        if (OrderProgress.IsTerminal(_stage))
        {
            return _stage == OrderStage.Cancelled
                ? "Final — no longer checking"
                : "Complete — no longer checking";
        }

        if (!_visible)
        {
            return "Paused while this tab is in the background";
        }

        if (_watchStopped)
        {
            return "Stopped checking after a long wait";
        }

        return _loading ? "Checking…" : "Checking for changes";
    }

    private string StatusTag() => _stage switch
    {
        OrderStage.Shipped => "vc-tag--sea",
        OrderStage.Paid or OrderStage.Packed => "vc-tag--brass",
        OrderStage.Cancelled => "vc-tag--signal",
        _ => "",
    };

    /// <summary>
    /// The link a shopper bookmarks: this page, not the API's own <c>retrievalPath</c>, carrying the
    /// same signed token. Absolute, because the point of it is to be pasted somewhere else.
    /// </summary>
    private string BookmarkUrl()
    {
        var origin = Nav.BaseUri.TrimEnd('/');
        var path = $"{origin}/order/{Uri.EscapeDataString(OrderNumber)}";

        return _bookmarkToken is { Length: > 0 } token
            ? $"{path}?token={Uri.EscapeDataString(token)}"
            : path;
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Selects the whole link when the field is focused, so copying it is one gesture rather than a
    /// drag across sixty characters of ciphertext. Wrapped, and a no-op when the module failed to
    /// import: the field is still selectable by hand, which is not worth an error for.
    /// </summary>
    private async Task SelectAllAsync()
    {
        if (_visibilityModule is null)
        {
            return;
        }

        try
        {
            await _visibilityModule.InvokeVoidAsync("selectAll", _linkField);
        }
        catch (Exception)
        {
            // Nothing to recover. The text is right there and selectable.
        }
    }

    private static string Money(MoneyDocument? money) =>
        money is null ? "—" : MoneyFormatter.Format(money.Amount, money.Currency);

    /// <summary>A date and time in the reader's own zone, for the one stamp that is not on the rail.</summary>
    private static string LongClock(DateTimeOffset instant) =>
        instant.ToLocalTime().ToString("d MMM yyyy, HH:mm", System.Globalization.CultureInfo.InvariantCulture);

    /// <summary>
    /// Stops the polling and unhooks JavaScript.
    /// <para>
    /// Every step is wrapped, because disposal usually runs while the shopper is navigating away and
    /// a JavaScript call at that moment may find the runtime already gone. A component that throws on
    /// the way out is a component that leaves the error bar over the page it was leaving for.
    /// </para>
    /// </summary>
    public async ValueTask DisposeAsync()
    {
        StopPolling();

        try
        {
            if (_visibilityModule is not null && _visibilityHandle is { } handle)
            {
                await _visibilityModule.InvokeVoidAsync("unwatch", handle);
            }

            if (_visibilityModule is not null)
            {
                await _visibilityModule.DisposeAsync();
            }
        }
        catch (Exception)
        {
            // The page is going away and so is the listener with it.
        }
        finally
        {
            _visibilityModule = null;
            _visibilityHandle = null;
            _self?.Dispose();
            _self = null;
        }
    }
}
